      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was hesitant to use \"flags\" in the name since I already have another member variable called flags and thought it might cause more confusion. Should I combine those flags also with a single uint32 variable val_flags?\n\nenum gpio_val_flags {\n  /* The flags will directly translate to their definition in gpio.h */\n  EC_GPIO_OPEN_DRAIN \u003d (1 \u003c\u003c 0)\n  EC_GPIO_PULL_UP \u003d (1 \u003c\u003c 1)\n  EC_GPIO_PULL_DOWN \u003d (1 \u003c\u003c 2)\n  EC_GPIO_ANALOG \u003d (1 \u003c\u003c 3)\n  EC_GPIO_INPUT \u003d (1 \u003c\u003c 4)\n  EC_GPIO_OUTPUT \u003d (1 \u003c\u003c 5)\n  EC_GPIO_LOW \u003d (1 \u003c\u003c 6)\n  EC_GPIO_HIGH \u003d (1 \u003c\u003c 7)\n  EC_GPIO_INT_F_RISING \u003d (1 \u003c\u003c 8)\n  EC_GPIO_INT_F_FALLING \u003d (1 \u003c\u003c 9)\n  EC_GPIO_INT_F_LOW \u003d (1 \u003c\u003c 11)\n  EC_GPIO_INT_F_HIGH \u003d (1 \u003c\u003c 12)\n  EC_GPIO_DEFAULT \u003d (1 \u003c\u003c 13)\n  EC_GPIO_INT_DSLEEP \u003d (1 \u003c\u003c 14)\n  /* For some possible additional states later on */\n\n  EC_GPIO_VAL_HIGH \u003d (1 \u003c\u003c 24)\n  EC_GPIO_VAL_CHANGED \u003d (1 \u003c\u003c 25)\n}",
