      "side": 1,
      "message": "Heh.  I found val_changed equally confusing, since (val_changed \u0026 EC_GPIO_VAL_HIGH) doesn\u0027t necessarily mean that the val has changed to be high.\n\nAre you reporting the flags as they are set for a GPIO at boot, or their current state?  If their current state, you can set either EC_GPIO_HIGH or EC_GPIO_LOW to indicate the current value.  Then we\u0027d just need one changed flag.\n\nChanged is also a bit weird in its implementation.  There\u0027s only one changed bit even though there are two ways to clear it - either with the host command or the console command.  So maybe we shouldn\u0027t attempt to report changed/clear via the host command at all.  Then you just need the one flags.",
